Thanks for the initiative calling!

Though I am not quite sure about some details of your proposal. Some
questions... (and I am asking for your/community's opinion of course)
1. What shall be the basis of further development?
   a) unfixed Vanilla 3.4.3
   b) the recently rewritten engine (without new features)
   c) any of the variants (with old engine) already existing
   d) to be defined by "The New Devteam"
   e) or something else?
2. What should be the "trade mark" of game and forum?
   a) nethack or something else?
   b) nethack.org (ask the Devteam?) or something else?
   c) an own name (from variant? or invented?)
   d) to be defined by "The New Devteam"
   e) something else?
3. How should game design and delivery times be decided?
   a) by one "single leader"
   b) by a circle of enlightened developers
   c) by "the community"
   d) tasks split to product managers, project leaders, developers
   e) something else?
4. What do you expect from a New Nethack that isn't present in the
   variants? (This is related to Q 1.)

What are you expecting from your posting?  To initiate such an effort
you need not be a developer, so don't hesitate to start organizing it;
contact the Devteam (if you think it might be necessary), contact the
variant developers, decide the code basis, propose the modus operandi,
etc. - there's a lot that you can already do to make it take off.

The variant developers have already done a step, an uncoordinated one.
You could do the coordination. And put development on a solid and long
lasting base. It's certainly no trivial project to focus all efforts.
And it probably will be a quite hard job deciding for a (single) game
philosophy with those many confident individualists. :-)

